# features/

One folder per feature. Every feature has the same fixed set of subfolders.

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

| Subfolder | What lives here | File suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [`ui/`](home/ui/) | Compose screens + screen-local composables | `*Screen.kt`, `*Section.kt` |
| [`viewmodel/`](home/viewmodel/) | `androidx.lifecycle.ViewModel` subclasses + UI state types | `*ViewModel.kt` |
| [`domain/`](home/domain/) | Pure-Kotlin business contracts: repository interfaces + use cases | `*Repository.kt`, `*UseCase.kt` |
| [`data/`](home/data/) | Repository implementations, Retrofit API interfaces, DTOs | `*RepositoryImpl.kt`, `*Api.kt` |

No file lives at the feature root — only the four subfolders + a `README.md`.

## What does NOT live here

- Cross-feature shared code → `core/`.
- Navigation graph → `navigation/`.
- The Application class / MainActivity → top-level package.

## Adding a new feature

Copy `_feature_template/`, rename, fill in the four subfolders. Add a route
in `navigation/AppNavGraph.kt`. Wire any new repository in
`core/di/AppGraph.kt`.

